From 9d993ee66251ebd21118fa7bbb6677a181ea5355 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:50:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] DC6C: OPT_DRAW_DIST and Combat detail (Smooth / Balanced
 / Max detail) on the PVR view, with the adaptive governor

The view's distance in cells is capped by the two Options rows (Near 12, Smooth 20, else 32) and
moved by the last drawn tick's work (main.c feeds it): over a mode's limit -3 cells, under its
comfort level +2. The first view after a scene change starts at 14 cells and grows, so the
level's load tick stays under 33.3 ms (COMBAT 0/1/2/4/6 entries: 5 ticks at 35.7-37.5 ms to 0,
worst 28.6 ms). Smooth also casts a sparse ray fan (4 columns a ray); Max detail makes more new
textures a view. Host tests for the rule, the caps, the options reaching the view and the feed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xd63cx9wuhKv8Rqec7pX14
